WEBVTT

00:03:29.697 --> 00:03:33.884
Our advances in understanding
protein folding

00:03:33.908 --> 00:03:35.630
and how to design proteins,

00:03:35.654 --> 00:03:39.282
coupled with the decreasing cost
of gene synthesis

00:03:39.306 --> 00:03:42.805
and the Moore's law increase
in computing power,

00:03:42.829 --> 00:03:47.565
now enable us to design
tens of thousands of new proteins,

00:03:47.589 --> 00:03:49.928
with new shapes and new functions,

00:03:49.952 --> 00:03:51.465
on the computer,

00:03:51.489 --> 00:03:55.404
and encode each one of those
in a synthetic gene.

00:03:56.248 --> 00:03:57.916
Once we have those synthetic genes,

00:03:57.940 --> 00:03:59.485
we put them into bacteria

00:03:59.509 --> 00:04:02.814
to program them to make
these brand-new proteins.